<!--
  /studio/_layout.sui — the studio chrome wrapper. Every route under
  /studio/* is wrapped in <ship-studio-chrome> (@ship/studio), which
  provides the studio rail + main content area + footer.

  The <slot name="route" /> is where the route content mounts. The
  host's `mountRoute(root, url, layouts, payload)` walks LAYOUTS,
  builds the chrome chain, and mounts the route content into the
  innermost <div slot="route">.

  <sui-shell-bottom> is a footer the hub does not ship; it renders as an
  unregistered custom element (no-op at runtime, no compile error). The
  hub's root layout (`routes/_layout.sui` → `<ship-app-chrome>`) supplies
  the real top nav outside the studio chrome.

  Height-chain integration: the mount-router's `buildMountTarget` appends
  this chrome to the outer root chrome (a custom element with a named
  `<slot name="route">`) as a light-DOM child. The chrome's controller sets
  `slot="route"` on its host in `mount`, which triggers slot redistribution
  and projects the chrome into the route slot — without that, the chrome
  would be unslotted light-DOM content and invisible inside the host's
  display. See @ship/studio's ship-studio-chrome.controller.ts.
-->

<ship-studio-chrome>
  <ship-studio-rail></ship-studio-rail>
  <main class="studio-main">
    <slot name="route" />
  </main>
  <sui-shell-bottom></sui-shell-bottom>
</ship-studio-chrome>
